From 2c49a96130da3157f29a2378f82d2702365aa476 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 04:33:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(digitizer): thread mislabeling bug + pro-parity
 harness truth pass
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two things landed together — an engine bug found while chasing a harness
question, and the harness itself getting fixed so the pro-comparison loop
measures something real.

THE ENGINE BUG (real, customer-visible, now fixed):
compact_layers keeps a palette slot for any layer that still holds a Region
- even one excluded from stitching (BACKGROUND_ENCLOSED, stitched=False).
StitchPlan.palette was built by passing that per-LAYER list straight through
and adapter._thread_name read it BY BLOCK INDEX. One phantom entry ahead of
a block and the block ships under the PREVIOUS cone's NAME while sewing with
its own correct thread NUMBER - invisible by eye because the stitches are
right, only the label is wrong. Measured: 22 of 96 blocks mislabeled across
6 of 23 real professional designs before the fix, 0 after. Zero stitches
changed (verified byte-identical output before/after on all 23).

Also: silent SHAPES_LEFT_UNSEWN (104 regions across 13 designs, intended
policy, now named with thread+area instead of invisible), a second
independent mismatch source flagged via new PALETTE_THREAD_MISMATCH
(revalidate_threads resnaps a shape's spool without updating its layer -
reported, not fixed; it's a sew-order product decision), and stage 5's
SHAPE_NOT_STITCHED now names the shape it drops instead of just counting.

THE HARNESS FIX (digitizer/tools/pro_parity/ - the pro-comparison scorecard):
Registration (designs now aligned before any overlap metric - machine_beanie
was scoring 0.22 coverage against a 26.6mm frame offset, corrected to 0.98),
coverage honesty (1mm+dilation was painting a 3mm swath - a 41%-density fill
scored 98% covered; now 0.125mm with an opacity gate), travel rewritten as
measured exposed drag in mm instead of a move-count proxy the engine could
evade by walking short steps, underlay made sequence-aware (a stitch is
underlay iff later covered by the SAME thread - kills phantom shares on both
sides), and source-art reconstruction fixed so letters don't get fused into
slabs by an oversized morphological close.

Net effect on the scorecard's own number: 66.1 -> 69.4 at shipped weights.
Not the simple "it was all inflated" story - coverage/underlay/density were
inflated (+2.7) but travel was DEFLATED (-3.1, the old metric over-counted
the PRO's own trimmed jumps as exposed travel). The real remaining distortion
is concentrated in direction/sttype, which sit near a 50% chance floor -
correcting for chance puts the honest number at 53.6, matching what the
original 23-design study predicted.

Zero stitch output changed by the engine fix (byte-identical on all 23
corpus designs, confirmed both before this commit and by re-running prep).
Digitizer suite: 1135 passed / 7 failed (same 7 pre-existing failures as
main - 5 need tesseract, 2 are platform-mismatch goldens), 3 skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
