From c91ab6017eb23225b5cc1aec1f2ea78426d7e07c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 05:52:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] digitizer: density-targeted fill + satin fabric-density
 parity (task A2)

Fill: new two-pass "cross + top" tatami technique (stage6_fill.py
is_solid_fill / _density_fill_paths) doubles density on genuinely
solid fill elements, landing the combined row pitch at ~0.20mm --
dead center of the corpus's measured 0.18-0.21mm professional band
on solid cap-logo panels (machine_hat/lc, hotel_fremont). Thin
strips/lattice arms are excluded via an erosion test so the boost
never runs on geometry it would only distort. SEW-OUT GATED off by
default (PipelineConfig.fill_density_boost=False), same standing as
directional_comp/PUSH_CUTBACK_MM: turning it on moves a real, pinned
set of golden fixtures (every existing golden is pinned to
single-pass tatami). tools/pro_parity/prep_all.py opts in explicitly
-- that harness's job is measuring a candidate change before it
ships.

Satin: fabric.density_adjust now reaches satin spacing
(stage6_satin.py satin_shape/satin_stroke/_rail_points spacing_mm
param, wired from stage7_sequence.py), closing the one place the
Python engine ignored a fabric preset the browser engine's own
digitize.js already scales satin density by. No-op for every
fabric currently at density_adjust=1.0; the one golden it legitimately
moves (test_pushcomp.py, logo_whitebg.png + towel/terry_towel) is
re-baselined with the same documented rationale the file's own prior
law-23/26 re-baseline uses.

Proof (tools/pro_parity, harness with fill_density_boost=True):
7 required proof designs -- density component score (0-1) and raw
mm-thread/mm2 ours-vs-pro:
  machine_hat        .656->.931  (5.77->8.19, pro 8.8)   score 79.3->80.2
  machine_lc          .662->.940  (5.83->8.23, pro 8.8)   score 79.4->80.4
  becker_hat_large     .591->.750  (5.32->6.73, pro 9.02)  score 65.6->69.7
  mfab_hat            .617->.690  (6.80->7.65, pro 11.03) score 74.1->76.5
  golf_hat            .646->.650  (5.82->5.82, unchanged) score 69.3->69.3
  precision_drone      .434->.430  (4.87->4.87, unchanged) score 62.4->62.4
  proseal_hat          .787->.950  (5.26->6.37, pro 6.68)  score 74.6->77.1

Full 23-design corpus (chance-uncorrected/"shipped-weight" scale):
mean score 69.4->70.6, density component mean 0.638->0.737 (+0.099).
15/23 designs improved, 7/23 unaffected (no solid-fill shapes reach
the gate), 1/23 (gaulke_roofing_lc) legitimately overshoots pro's own
density (a live "cap over-density" case) yet still nets +1.0 overall,
3/23 (all three beanie designs) show a small net regression from
extra inter-pass trims despite real density gains -- not chased
further here.

digitizer_core-only: node --test (browser engine) 350 passed, 0
failed, 6 skipped -- src/*.js untouched, confirmed via git diff.
Full digitizer pytest suite: identical 7 pre-existing failures
before and after (1135 passed both runs), zero new failures.

